  "reason": "The current best (config_037: scVI, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.706 acc. The evidence strongly supports multiprofile, avgpool aggregation, weighted fusion, and ViT-L as the optimal settings for all parameters except the RNA encoder. The RNA encoder axis shows clear progression (PCA 0.639 → scVI 0.678), but scGPT is completely untested in the multimodal setting. Config_049 (scGPT, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) isolates the scGPT variable while holding all other parameters at their best-known values, directly testing whether a more advanced generative RNA encoder can outperform scVI. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-value experiment: if scGPT exceeds scVI it yields a new best configuration; if it underperforms, it confirms scVI as the optimal encoder and redirects budget toward other refinements (e.g., transformer aggregation re-test or fusion variants). No other untested configuration addresses such a large unexplored dimension under otherwise optimal settings."
